body:
Refs #1088. Decision 0109, slice 0109a1: the record. A gate's findings, the head it covered and the head its check accepted are engine-stamped seat-record v7 fields, and decide reads one journaled observation per protected effect.

Brokkr-Run: landing-over-an-existing-branch--3d2e9264
Ruling: #1088 (https://github.com/feedback-loop-ai/brokkr/issues/1088#issuecomment-6960606249), operator 2026-11-17, "accept 0109 as recommended": decision 0109 accepted with its 13 rulings as recommended; this PR builds slice 0109a1.
Ruling: #1088 (https://github.com/feedback-loop-ai/brokkr/issues/1088#issuecomment-7061728507), operator 2026-11-21, "1.a 2. 50 MB": the threat-model frame is (a), the account is the trust root for direct journal writes; and the binary size ceiling is 50 MB, raised in this PR by be40c783b.
Ruling: #1088 (https://github.com/feedback-loop-ai/brokkr/issues/1088#issuecomment-7048314178), operator standing ruling 2026-11-04, "go with recommended on anything else that comes up" and "and by hand". It covers:
- the 0109a1/0109a2 split;
- fix rounds r2 to r8, and the landing re-seated off two failed providers;
- the controller's by-hand coverage, complexity and mutant fixes, and the restack;
- the public API growth:
  - brokkr-core +124 (the `findings` module);
  - brokkr-store +4 (`SeatRecordVersion::V7`, `SeatRecordError::settled_member`, `Store::envelopes_of_checkpoints`, `Store::envelopes_of_member_markers`);
  - brokkr-view +22 (`GateRecord`, `GateFinding`, `gate_records`, `gate_records_within`, `verdict_attempts_within`);
- the #1212 follow-ups folded in: 1212a's L2 and carry commits, landing `landing-over-an-existing-branch--b7dd3c4d`'s fix rounds, and the controller's 117395b3b. The landing chief's PR asks are taken as recommended and listed under Asks;
- FROZEN 39 → 40, which pins seat-record v6 beside the new v7;
- the Callgrind regression (c-7061668662): `inspect fixture_run` +14.0% against base 04b20b455 (23,826,124 → 27,167,839 instructions; it was +33.6% before the #1212 follow-ups), accepted as the verdicts block's own cost within the 1,000-row budget. The SQL marker prefilter that would cut it is a follow-up on #1212 (c-7061670779).

It lands re-signed, with the `by-hand` label.

**Ready.** CI run 44899709734 on b35c9fd2d is green except CPU budgets: `inspect fixture_run` +14.0%, ruled in c-7061668662. The release binary is within the 50 MB ceiling, and `delivered by brokkr` passes. The mutants workflow's report-only `brokkr-protocol` job fails on its unmutated baseline (hands-box tests in the runner), as it did on 117395b3b. Its `brokkr-core` gate passes. The operator ruled both asks on 2026-11-21 (#1088 c-7061728507).

**The gap 1221a r1 found, fixed by b35c9fd2d** (c-7057813579): bb7a73b67 parked a protected sequence's pre-gate `security-hold` (`Unrecorded`), where 0050 rulings 5 and 7 and 0109's "What stays out" say it stops. The shipped `recipes/gpt-flash` hit it, because its work-class `positions` panel may end on the hold. decide now takes a compiled pre-gate hard stop on no head: no reviewed head and no ship request, with every other refusal and its text unchanged. `verdict/stop_tests.rs` runs shipped gpt-flash through the real engine: the hold stops the run before its chief, and the clean twin decides on the chief's record.

## What it builds

**Seat-record v7** (`contracts/seat-record.v7.schema.json`) is written by every 0.14+ result and checkpoint row.
- Both `covered` arms are in the schema; only `head` is written. `dirty` is `true` on every record until 0109b's tree check.
- The `artifacts` arm and `follow_ups` are admitted by the schema and written by no path until 0109c and 0109d.
- v6 is frozen.

**Findings** (`brokkr-core::findings`):
- `Finding` and `FindingKey`, stamped by the engine with the reporting site.
- One shared admission (`admit`, `admit_live`) refuses three things:
  - a seat-supplied `covered`, `checked_head`, `follow_ups` or `site`;
  - findings from a work site;
  - any finding in a driver's live checkpoint.
- `line` and `file` are closed, and a `null` line is refused.

**One observation per protected effect (0109 ruling 7):**
- the head a gate's check accepted is journaled durably as `checked_head`;
- a sequence's gate steps journal their own authored step records;
- decide reads them from the fold and refuses when an observation is missing, partial, malformed, reordered or disagreeing (`Disagrees`, `Unrecorded`, `Uncovered`, `Reordered`, `Unlawful`, `Unselected`);
- the terminal never chooses its own obligations. Its lawful positions and its digest form come from the compiled body, and a body with a gate decides on the latest whole gate record's head (M1 to M3).

**Settled members:**
- the engine marks a member's payload with `authored: engine`, and an unmarked payload reads as unverified legacy evidence;
- a marked payload is validated as a standalone result at append, export and verify;
- a refused member is named as typed data and removed alone, so its siblings keep their verdicts and retry eligibility (X4, M4);
- every settled payload, a held terminal included, takes one bounded per-member append path (M5).

**Inspect** reads a gate's findings and covered head back, through a scoped, repair-aware verdicts block. `VIEW_VERSION` stays 32, since `GateRecord` is off the wire.

**Inspect's verdicts within the frame's budget** (#1212 L2, folded in):
- Plain `inspect` reads its verdicts from the newest 1,000 rows up to the frame's head (0089 ruling 9). The frame's trail is handed over with no second read.
- Any cut is always printed, so it is never silent.
- A verdict whose attempt began before the window still shows. A panel member's authored finish before the window is read by attempt, in one query, as context.
- `--phase`, `--seat` and an index-less journal read the run whole, as before.
- The partial-retry carry reads a sequence step's record by the engine's authorship, never by its word.

## Review

The landing's panel was:
- DeepSeek Flash, adversarial;
- Claude Opus 5.5, correctness;
- DeepSeek Flash, correctness.

The Claude Opus 5.5 chief ruled REVIEW-RESIDUAL-OK, with no security residual and no specification defect. The chief's own read confirmed M1 to M5. The unit held seven times before this, and every round is recorded on #1088.

**Its one surviving LOW and three carried items went to #1212:**
- **L1, re-scoped** (#1221 c-7057813015): the engine takes a compiled pre-gate hard stop, and the compiler refuses only a pre-gate ending on a word that does not stop the run. Its engine half, 1221a2's item 1a, is in here as b35c9fd2d. The compiler half (1b) is in 1221a's PR, stacked on #1222.
- **L2, inspect's verdicts within the frame's budget:** folded in.
- **The carry marker reader by authorship:** folded in. The cool-down reader is 0106b1's and stays on #1212.
- **The thin `Box<str>`:** dropped. Its premise was wrong: `Box<String>` is already thin, at 8 B.

**The #1212 landing** (`landing-over-an-existing-branch--b7dd3c4d`, the same panel and an Opus chief) ended on REVIEW-REFORGE-EXHAUSTED-DEBT at 40792f47a: residual, max `low`, no security residual and no specification defect (#1212 c-7060358484). Its three LOW findings:
- **R1, fixed in 117395b3b:** the attempts' member markers were read one query per attempt.
- **R3, fixed in 117395b3b:** the store test now writes the markers through `EngineMarker`.
- **R2, open:** at or under the budget, the frame and its verdicts read in two passes. The second whole `Store::load` is gone, but each checkpoint is still read by key. This PR's Callgrind re-measures it.

## Asks

**Ruled by the operator, 2026-11-21** (#1088 c-7061728507, "1.a 2. 50 MB"):
- **The threat-model frame: (a).** The account is the trust root for direct journal writes, as 0111 S1 and 0046 ruling 4 say.
  - 0109's checks guard seat payloads through the driver protocol, recipe authors and engine paths, and stay as integrity refusals.
  - A finding that needs a direct journal write by a process of the account does not hold a slice.
  - The code is the same either way.
- **The binary size ceiling: 50 MB**, raised here by be40c783b (`quality/binary-size.json`, its note's history and measurements updated).
  - CI's release build of this PR is 40,180,440 bytes at 117395b3b, and 40,341,608 at f26bccaea.
  - Main at 04b20b45 is 39,664,328.
  - #1222, stacked on this PR, builds 40,382,456.

**Taken as recommended under the standing ruling:**
- v7's records and arms as above;
- the one head observation and its durable seam, `HeadReads`;
- an unclassed dialect step compiles as a gate (`bundle/sequence.rs::step_class`);
- the work-site and live-finding refusals;
- the fence's typed read, and `SeatRecordError` kept typed through the sequence helpers;
- K5's boundary, the within-row `authored: engine` fact. Released 0.14.0 and 0.15.0 wrote v6-era rows, and `V7_ENGINE` documents both;
- V2/W6's mark and the unverified legacy reading, on direct reads and on carry;
- W4's per-scope reading of an admitted finding inside a refused aggregate;
- X1's compiled observation set, the bound producer identity, the latched malformed record and the audit list;
- M1's compiled terminal position and gate-record head;
- M2's compiled digest form;
- M3's order rule;
- M4's typed member identity;
- the API growth and FROZEN above;
- **the #1212 landing chief's asks, as built:**
  - the 1,000-row verdicts budget (0089 ruling 9);
  - the elision line ("the first N were not read") prints on every run over the budget, even when no verdict was cut. That over-discloses, which is the safe direction;
  - `--json` prints no verdicts block, as before, and `--phase` and `--seat` read the run whole before applying their lens;
  - a 0.14 or 0.15 step record carries no `authored`. A run parked mid-sequence and resumed by this build re-runs its finished steps, which fails safe.

**Moved files:** prompt assertions and `quality/prompt-bytes.json` moved with the adapters.rs prompt sentence, and no witness digest changed. The witness journal golden gained `authored`.

**FROZEN:** 39 → 40 here. Main's #1208 (decision 0112's `effect-usage.v1`) took it from 38 to 39 first, so the restack moved the count. The commit that pins v6 says "39 to 40" (the reviewed text said "38 to 39"). That is the one commit message the restack changed. 0106b1 also moves FROZEN's length, so whichever of the two lands second reconciles it.

## Checked by the controller

**At head b35c9fd2d,** 1a (b35c9fd2d) on the ceiling (be40c783b): runtime lib 2,375 tests and engine::verdict 53, workspace clippy `--all-targets --all-features -D warnings`, typos, and the files, clones and api ratchets. In 1221a's tree, the host's exact coverage measured 1a at 100%.

**At head 117395b3b** (the #1212 follow-ups on f26bccaea):
- host exact coverage: lines, branches and functions all 100% (102,432 lines, 12,562 branches, 13,650 functions);
- the host lints, the api ratchet included;
- fmt, and workspace clippy `--all-targets -D warnings`;
- the evidence: `brokkr-runs/landing-over-an-existing-branch--b7dd3c4d`;
- every commit signed.

The core is unchanged since f26bccaea, so the core mutants gate below still stands.

**Before the follow-ups:**

On the tree restacked onto main 4b0c3a9b0, at head 4f2edc870:
- host exact coverage: lines, branches and functions all 100% (102,079 lines, 12,540 branches, 13,589 functions);
- the host lints: typos, the files, clones, crap and api ratchets, shellcheck and actionlint;
- fmt, and workspace clippy `--all-targets --all-features -D warnings`;
- the core mutants gate (`scripts/mutants.sh gate origin/main brokkr-core`): 115 mutants, 88 caught, 27 unviable, 0 missed;
- 66 commits, every one signed. Authors and messages are byte-identical to the reviewed ones, except the FROZEN count above;
- runtime (2,360) and store (694) lib tests, and `frozen_contracts` (28), on the merged tree.

Then a third, one-line restack onto c1a65839f (#1207, #1211) gives head f26bccaea. It merges clean with main 04b20b455 (#1214), and the two share no files. Checked there: fmt, workspace clippy, and brokkr-cli's lib tests plus the readout, witness, lifecycle and graph integration tests (1,476 lib tests, 30 integration tests).

**The restack** went in three passes.

The first, onto 659aed440, had three conflicts:
- `render.rs`: main's `mod graph` kept beside the unit's `pub(crate) mod inspect`;
- `quickstart.md` and `read-surfaces.md`: main's #1168 glyphs kept, plus the unit's verdicts elision.

`chain.rs` auto-merged, with main's statement cache and `patiently` path in separate hunks.

The second, onto 4b0c3a9b0 after #1208, #1209 and #1210, had five conflicts:
- `contracts/README.md`: 0112's effect-usage section kept, then the unit's seat-record v7 section;
- `frozen_contracts.rs`: the v6 pin added beside 0112's, with the count at 40;
- `engine.rs`: main's `mod usage` beside the unit's `mod verdict`;
- `panel.rs` and `sequence.rs`: the unit's `(reports, stamped)` return, plus main's `self.usage.panel(…)` and `panel_step(…)` reading the same reports.

The third pass, onto c1a65839f after #1207 and #1211, had one conflict: `render.rs` keeps main's `style` and `table` modules, with `inspect` as `pub(crate)`.

0112's `usage` sits beside `result` in the effect payload, and v7 closes only the seat record inside `result`, so neither reads the other. Per file, the unit's changed lines are identical before and after, except FROZEN's count.

**By-hand commits after the landing:**
- 580678539 (core) and 5a1b71a1a (runtime): the exact gate's eight unreached edges (3 lines, 5 branches), test only;
- a1dd38462, the complexity fix: `Engine::execute_with` from CC 16 to 13, via `arm_observation`, with no behaviour change;
- f26bccaea, the mutant fix: `Finding::security`'s survivor caught.

